    {
      "id": "t0192",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 78,
      "y": 2820.5234375,
      "width": 996.5999999999999,
      "height": 137.5,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#212529",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "g0189"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 905470947,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1741543656,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CACHING - every derived thing is content-addressed and lives in S3: the GLT, the masked observation, the ortho and aux warps, the epoch snapshot,\nthe product block. Verbatim DAAC granules are the one exception and stay node-local, because an unmodified copy in S3 buys nothing. So a re-run resumes\nonto whatever survived, and widening the window to 2026 re-reads the 2025 snapshots instead of recomputing them - as long as the scorer, the masks and\nthe schema still hash the same. That last clause is the whole contract.\n\nMEASURED, not estimated, against CMR on 17 Sep 2026:   1,932 granules · 402 tiles · 9,233 regrid · 87,479 resolve · 10,050 reduce · 402 publish\n                                                       ~442 GB in · ~845 GB of S3 at peak · ~$33-92 of Lambda · ~85-193 CPU-hours\n\nBoxes are clickable: each links to the code or the manifest line that implements it, pinned at 5688e8d so the line numbers stay true.\nGenerated from examples/emit-us-west-2025/manifest.yaml - and then hand-edited, so this file is the source of truth, not the generator.",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "CACHING - every derived thing is content-addressed and lives in S3: the GLT, the masked observation, the ortho and aux warps, the epoch snapshot,\nthe product block. Verbatim DAAC granules are the one exception and stay node-local, because an unmodified copy in S3 buys nothing. So a re-run resumes\nonto whatever survived, and widening the window to 2026 re-reads the 2025 snapshots instead of recomputing them - as long as the scorer, the masks and\nthe schema still hash the same. That last clause is the whole contract.\n\nMEASURED, not estimated, against CMR on 17 Sep 2026:   1,932 granules · 402 tiles · 9,233 regrid · 87,479 resolve · 10,050 reduce · 402 publish\n                                                       ~442 GB in · ~845 GB of S3 at peak · ~$33-92 of Lambda · ~85-193 CPU-hours\n\nBoxes are clickable: each links to the code or the manifest line that implements it, pinned at 5688e8d so the line numbers stay true.\nGenerated from examples/emit-us-west-2025/manifest.yaml - and then hand-edited, so this file is the source of truth, not the generator.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
