    },
    {
      "id": "tv20119",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 875.97265625,
      "y": 1326.0,
      "width": 352.8,
      "height": 435.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#212529",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 682281553,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 730160159,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "BARE EARTH IS pv <= 0.40 (24 Sep science tag-up).\nNPV is not reliable enough to use, so the\nbare-soil fraction (1 - pv - npv) and its 0.65\nfloor are gone. A greener look is GRADED to a\ntenth, not refused: it still loses to any bare\nlook in its week, and it still votes across the\nyear at a tenth of a bare week's strength.\n\nvegetated_weight must stay under 0.60 / (0.60 +\n0.25 + 0.10) = 0.63, ENFORCED in the constructor,\nor a green look could outrank a bare one.\nsun_weight + nadir_weight <= 1 is enforced the\nsame way, so the tie-breakers never outrank\ncover.\n\nSNOW needs no rule. FRCOV writes fill into every\nfraction wherever its QC band flags cloud, urban,\nwater or snow/ice (NDSI > 0.4), and fill makes\nthe look invalid before it is scored.\n\nWhy 15°: EMIT's view zenith spans only a few\ndegrees, so normalising over 0-90° would make the\nnadir term numerically irrelevant.\n\nMeasured with the earlier bare-soil scorer, one\ntile over 2025: the nadir term recovers 0.36° of\nmean view zenith and changes the mineral label on\n0.08 % of cells - a TILE-CONTINUITY knob, not a\ncorrectness fix.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "BARE EARTH IS pv <= 0.40 (24 Sep science tag-up).\nNPV is not reliable enough to use, so the\nbare-soil fraction (1 - pv - npv) and its 0.65\nfloor are gone. A greener look is GRADED to a\ntenth, not refused: it still loses to any bare\nlook in its week, and it still votes across the\nyear at a tenth of a bare week's strength.\n\nvegetated_weight must stay under 0.60 / (0.60 +\n0.25 + 0.10) = 0.63, ENFORCED in the constructor,\nor a green look could outrank a bare one.\nsun_weight + nadir_weight <= 1 is enforced the\nsame way, so the tie-breakers never outrank\ncover.\n\nSNOW needs no rule. FRCOV writes fill into every\nfraction wherever its QC band flags cloud, urban,\nwater or snow/ice (NDSI > 0.4), and fill makes\nthe look invalid before it is scored.\n\nWhy 15°: EMIT's view zenith spans only a few\ndegrees, so normalising over 0-90° would make the\nnadir term numerically irrelevant.\n\nMeasured with the earlier bare-soil scorer, one\ntile over 2025: the nadir term recovers 0.36° of\nmean view zenith and changes the mineral label on\n0.08 % of cells - a TILE-CONTINUITY knob, not a\ncorrectness fix.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
