      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": null,
      "text": "mineral_family\n@ref:mineral-family-v1\nthe same rows, cut differently",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "xC7dvDCLuIC_2MvYqsFzM",
      "originalText": "mineral_family\n@ref:mineral-family-v1\nthe same rows, cut differently",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
    {
      "id": "tv20121",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1338,
      "y": 1544.0,
      "width": 1008.0,
      "height": 120.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#212529",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 545625652,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 118321417,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "THREE GROUPINGS OVER THE SAME DETECTIONS, each an independent enumeration and an independent vote. None is privileged; a fourth is a YAML\nfile. \"The only way to do this is to basically flood it and give multiple different groupings available.\"  The ungrouped 294-class layers\nship BESIDE the groupings, not instead of them, because a picture of the raw detections is what tells you whether a grouping threw something\naway.\n\nNO GROUP-1 / GROUP-2 TRADE.  joint_mineral_vote would answer a cell from group 2 where group 2 voted and from group 1 where it did not. The\n17 Sep tag-up ruled that out: \"the detections between group one and group 2 are independent from one another... you cannot swap in a group 2\nif a group one is absent.\"  Two mosaics, never one.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "THREE GROUPINGS OVER THE SAME DETECTIONS, each an independent enumeration and an independent vote. None is privileged; a fourth is a YAML\nfile. \"The only way to do this is to basically flood it and give multiple different groupings available.\"  The ungrouped 294-class layers\nship BESIDE the groupings, not instead of them, because a picture of the raw detections is what tells you whether a grouping threw something\naway.\n\nNO GROUP-1 / GROUP-2 TRADE.  joint_mineral_vote would answer a cell from group 2 where group 2 voted and from group 1 where it did not. The\n17 Sep tag-up ruled that out: \"the detections between group one and group 2 are independent from one another... you cannot swap in a group 2\nif a group one is absent.\"  Two mosaics, never one.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "tv20122",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1338,
      "y": 1786.0,
      "width": 1000.8,
      "height": 60.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#212529",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 649187324,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1998679710,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CATEGORICAL - vote, weighted by score.  The voting unit is still the EPOCH: a week with four looks casts ONE vote, cast by the look the\nscorer liked best - but the vote now weighs what that look scored, so one bare week outweighs about ten vegetated ones. A class backed by a\nbare week is reported on its own; one seen only through vegetation needs three agreeing weeks. _agreement, the winner's share of the total\nscore, is the confidence.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "CATEGORICAL - vote, weighted by score.  The voting unit is still the EPOCH: a week with four looks casts ONE vote, cast by the look the\nscorer liked best - but the vote now weighs what that look scored, so one bare week outweighs about ten vegetated ones. A class backed by a\nbare week is reported on its own; one seen only through vegetation needs three agreeing weeks. _agreement, the winner's share of the total\nscore, is the confidence.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
